{"created": "2026-08-09T17:52:00.629426+00:00", "modified": "2026-08-09T17:52:01.051513+00:00", "id": 21863461, "conceptrecid": "18968481", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21863461", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.18968481", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21863461", "metadata": {"title": "The Canonical Form of Attention: Positive Geometry, SYK Vertices, and Superconformal Symmetry in Transformer Architectures", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21863461", "publication_date": "2026-08-09", "description": "<p><strong>ERRATUM (August 9, 2026).</strong> Section 8.3&rsquo;s entropy-gap formula (H_gap = 2&Delta;&middot;log n for a normalized power-law attention distribution) is mathematically incorrect: the entropy gap of a normalized power law with exponent 2&Delta; &lt; 1 converges to a constant, and its slope against log n over the paper&rsquo;s own measured range is an order of magnitude below the formula&rsquo;s prediction (0.041 versus 0.50 at &Delta; = 1/4). The error drops the energy term s&middot;E[log r] from the entropy. Consequently the entropic estimate &Delta;_eff = 0.254 (Section 8.3), the k_eff &prop; n^(1&minus;2&Delta;) derivation (Section 8.4), and the abstract-level claim that <em>two independent observables measure one exponent to 1.4%</em> are <strong>withdrawn</strong>. The Section 8 measurements themselves (logarithmic entropy-gap growth, R&sup2; &gt; 0.97; the measured k_eff scaling) stand as measurements, but they measure n-independent concentration structure, not the conformal dimension. The paper&rsquo;s exact results (the canonical-form identity, the quartic vertex, the perturbative identity H_gap = &frac12;Var(s)) and the direct power-law profile measurements are unaffected. Full correction, correct algebra, numerical demonstration, affected-statement list, and the self-contained verification script are in <code>canonical_form_erratum.pdf</code> and <code>k1_powerlaw_gap.py</code>, added in this version. The original paper PDF is retained unchanged; this program corrects the record by dated erratum, not by silent revision.</p><p>v4: Corrected Maldacena-Stanford (2016) title from 'Remarks' to 'Comments'.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Ariel", "affiliation": "Independent research, in collaboration with Eldon Umphrey"}], "version": "v5 (erratum)", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 4, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "18968481"}}]}}, "title": "The Canonical Form of Attention: Positive Geometry, SYK Vertices, and Superconformal Symmetry in Transformer Architectures", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21863461", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21863461", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21863461?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21863461", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21863461", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21863461", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21863461/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/18968481", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/18968481", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18968481", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.18968481", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21863461/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21863461/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21863461/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21863461/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21863461:canonical_form_paper.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21863461:canonical_form_paper.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21863461:canonical_form_paper.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api